WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们带来终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

8
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:26.940
Oh, and welcome back to Office Ladies.
哦，欢迎回到《办公室女士》。

9
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.960
This week, we are breaking down The Job Part 2.
本周，我们要剖析的是《工作》下集。

10
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:37.780
It's the season three finale, second half, written by Paul Lieberstein and Mike Schur, directed by Ken Kuapis.
这是第三季的季终集，下半部分，由保罗·李伯斯坦和迈克·舒尔编剧，肯·夸皮斯执导。

11
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.400
Last week, we interviewed Paul Lieberstein, a.k.a.
上周，我们采访了保罗·李伯斯坦，也就是托比，

12
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.200
Toby, about this episode.
聊了聊这一集。

13
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:43.940
It was great.
太棒了。

14
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:44.800
So fun.
非常有趣。

15
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.120
So fun to talk to him.
和他聊天真开心。

16
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.420
Well, this week, we're going to break down the second half.
那么本周，我们要剖析下半部分。

17
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.360
And I've got a summary to catch us up.
我准备了一份摘要来帮我们回顾一下。

18
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.560
Well, Jenna, you know I can't wait to hear it.
珍娜，你知道我迫不及待想听了。

19
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:56.400
I know.
我知道。

20
00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.700
Now, do you really like my summaries, Angela?
安吉拉，你真的喜欢我的摘要吗？

21
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.740
I actually really do.
我确实很喜欢。

22
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.900
Now, that probably sounded like I was being some BFF sass to you.
刚才那听起来可能像是我在跟你开闺蜜玩笑。

23
00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.160
But I actually really do because you're so good at summarizing them.
但我确实是真心的，因为你真的很擅长总结剧情。

24
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:14.840
I think you might have missed your calling as like someone who writes the caption for movies, you know?
我觉得你可能错过了你的职业方向，比如去给电影写简介什么的，你知道吗？

25
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.240
Like the little slogan.
就像那种小标语。

26
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.880
The thing that comes up on your TV guide?
就是电视节目指南上显示的那种？

27
00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:19.460
Yes.
对。

28
00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:20.500
Yes.
没错。

29
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:24.100
I think you could have been that person, except for look who's talking.
我觉得你完全能胜任，不过话说回来，这还真是五十步笑百步。

30
00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:30.970
That made me laugh out loud.
那句话让我大笑出声。

31
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:31.530
I know.
我知道。

32
00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:32.030
I gotcha.
我懂你。

33
00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:32.430
As y'all heard.
正如大家所听到的。

34
00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.890
Okay, so give us a summary.
好了，给我们讲讲摘要吧。

35
00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:34.850
All right.
好的。

36
00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:41.530
Last week, we discussed how Michael got back together with Jan after she revealed her breast enhancement.
上周，我们讨论了迈克尔在简透露她做了隆胸手术后，是如何与她复合的。

37
00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:48.650
He named Dwight as his successor to Dunder Mifflin because he was so sure he was going to get this job at corporate.
他任命德怀特为邓德·米夫林公司的继任者，因为他确信自己能得到总部的那个职位。

38
00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.550
But I have just pause one second here.
但我得先暂停一下。

39
00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.450
Is that even Michael's decision to make?
这真的是迈克尔能决定的吗？

40
00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.730
We did not talk about this.
我们之前没讨论过这个。

41
00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:05.130
I mean, if Michael gets the job at corporate, is he allowed to just say who gets the manager job at Dunder Mifflin Scranton?
我是说，如果迈克尔得到了总部的职位，他有权直接指定谁来担任邓德·米夫林斯克兰分公司的经理吗？

42
00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.630
No, no, absolutely not.
不，不，绝对没有。

43
00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:14.810
I'm sure that's like a corporate decision where they like have an overview of all and, you know, all the employees.
我敢肯定那是公司高层的决定，他们会对所有员工进行全面评估。

44
00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.650
I'm sure Michael gets to put in his recommendation as someone that worked in that branch.
我确信迈克尔可以作为在该分公司工作过的人提出建议。

45
00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:21.790
But ultimately, that would be David Wallace's decision.
但最终，那应该是大卫·华莱士的决定。

46
00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:23.410
Thank you.
谢谢你。

47
00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.850
I feel like we failed to discuss that last week and I needed to bring it up.
我觉得我们上周没讨论到这一点，我必须提出来。

48
00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:28.450
Well, I gotcha.
好吧，我懂了。

49
00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:29.850
Done and done.
搞定。

50
00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:30.490
All right.
好的。

51
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:36.530
So, also last week, Dwight interviewed Andy to be his number two and Jim and Karen left for New York.
上周，德怀特面试了安迪，想让他当自己的副手，而吉姆和凯伦出发去了纽约。

52
00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:37.350
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

53
00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:44.150
This week, Pam is going to become Dwight's secret assistant to the regional manager.
这周，帕姆将成为德怀特这位区域经理的秘密助理。

54
00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:52.850
We will see Michael, Jim, and Karen all interview for the position at corporate and we will ultimately find out who gets the job.
我们将看到迈克尔、吉姆和凯伦都去参加了总部的职位面试，最终也会揭晓谁得到了这份工作。

55
00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:54.030
Yes.
没错。

56
00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.890
There's some relationship stuff thrown in there, too.
其中还穿插了一些感情戏。

57
00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.570
But, you know.
不过，你知道的。

58
00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:02.750
There's a little bit, isn't there, of relationship stuff.
确实有一点感情戏，不是吗？

59
00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.050
All right.
好吧。

60
00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.810
Fast fact number one, fan question from Maddie Jensen.
速览事实一，来自粉丝麦迪·詹森的提问。

61
00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:13.850
I noticed that Ken Kwapis directed the finale for season three along with the finale of season two.
我注意到肯·夸皮斯执导了第三季的季终集，同时也执导了第二季的季终集。

62
00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:18.290
Both episodes are crucial to the Jim-Pam plotline of the show.
这两集对剧中吉姆和帕姆的情感线至关重要。

63
00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:25.290
Was this an intentional decision to have the same director in charge of these important episodes or was it just a happy accident?
让同一位导演执导这些重要剧集是有意为之，还是纯属巧合？

64
00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.230
Well, this was very intentional.
嗯，这绝对是有意为之。

65
00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:30.990
I'm so glad you said that because I was sitting here and I wasn't sure.
真高兴你这么说，因为我刚才坐在这儿还不确定呢。

66
00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.450
I was like, what is she going to say?
我当时心想，她会怎么说呢？

67
00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:40.890
And I was like, I hope it was thought out because Ken was so caring about the different dynamics and relationships on the show.
我希望这是经过深思熟虑的，因为肯非常关心剧中不同的人物动态和关系。

68
00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.270
He had been with us since the pilot.
他从试播集开始就一直和我们在一起。

69
00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.730
We had such a trust for his vision.
我们非常信任他的愿景。

70
00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:49.650
And if you were about to say, it was just a scheduling thing, I was going to be like, no.
如果你刚才要说是档期安排的原因，我肯定会反驳说，才不是呢。

71
00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:59.530
No, I traded some emails with Ken Zabornak, and he told me that he and Greg always wanted Ken Kwapis to direct milestone episodes.
不，我和肯·扎博纳克通过几次邮件，他告诉我，他和格雷格一直希望由肯·夸皮斯来执导里程碑式的剧集。

72
00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:08.350
So season openers, season closers, or any episodes with big story movement, especially if they involve Jim and Pam.
比如季首集、季终集，或者任何有重大剧情推进的剧集，尤其是涉及吉姆和帕姆的那些。

73
00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.450
He wasn't always available, but that was the intention.
他并不总是有空，但初衷确实如此。

74
00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:24.470
And if you look back, Ange, you'll see that oftentimes it was Ken Kwapis, Greg Daniels, Paul Feig, or Paul Lieberstein who would direct these big milestone episodes,
如果你回过头看，安吉，你会发现很多时候都是肯·夸皮斯、格雷格·丹尼尔斯、保罗·费格或保罗·利伯斯坦在执导这些重大的里程碑剧集，

75
00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:31.370
which makes sense because those guys were kind of the original team of visionaries for the show.
这很合理，因为他们算是这部剧最初的愿景团队。

76
00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.930
And they were with us since the first season.
而且他们从第一季开始就一直和我们在一起。

77
00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:38.270
Yeah, so they knew every character's journey, and I think that was super important.
没错，所以他们了解每个角色的心路历程，我觉得这非常重要。

78
00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:41.510
That was sometimes a learning curve for new directors.
对于新导演来说，这有时需要一个学习过程。

79
00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:49.690
If they hadn't seen every single episode, they would come in and maybe not understand why a character was making a certain choice.
如果他们没看过每一集，他们进来时可能就无法理解为什么某个角色会做出某种选择。

80
00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:53.210
And I remember the cast would sometimes just bring them up to speed.
我记得演员们有时会主动帮他们补课。

81
00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:54.350
Oh, I did.
哦，我就做过。

82
00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.670
I remember I was in the scene.
我记得当时我在拍一场戏。

83
00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.770
I forget who the director was, but they were like, so let's have Angela over there, like, cutting the meat or something.
我不记得导演是谁了，但他们说，让安吉拉在那边切肉什么的。

84
00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:03.490
It was like a party episode.
那是一场派对戏。

85
00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.250
And I was like, oh, she wouldn't touch that meat.
我就说，哦，她才不会碰那块肉。

86
00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:06.070
She's a vegetarian.
她是素食主义者。

87
00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:07.770
She wouldn't go near it.
她根本不会靠近那东西。

88
00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:08.810
Yes.
没错。

89
00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.510
And they're like, oh, okay, I guess I'll put you over there by the bag of chips.
然后他们就说，哦，好吧，那我把你安排在那袋薯片旁边吧。

90
00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:13.610
I'm like, yes, that's better.
我说，太好了，那样更好。

91
00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:15.270
Exactly.
正是如此。

92
00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:23.710
So this created a really nice sense of consistency for those big episodes to bring people back who knew us all so well.
所以，让那些非常了解我们的人回归来执导这些大剧集，确实营造出了一种非常好的连贯感。

93
00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:24.530
All right.
好吧。

94
00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.530
Fast fact number two.
速览事实二。

95
00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:35.250
This is a fan question from Beatrix Smith, Brooke B., Amelia C., Erica P., and Supa Nanduri.
这是一个来自比阿特丽克斯·史密斯、布鲁克·B、阿米莉亚·C、埃里卡·P和苏帕·南杜里的粉丝提问。

96
00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:46.190
Did the conversation at the beach between Jim and Pam that we see throughout this episode, did it have to be recreated like the kiss on casino night?
我们在这一集中看到的吉姆和帕姆在海滩上的对话，是像赌场之夜的吻戏那样重新拍摄的吗？

97
00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:50.350
Or was it a deleted scene that was added later without audio?
还是说那是一段后来补进去的无声删减片段？

98
00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.510
What's the story?
背后的故事是什么？

99
00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:56.250
Well, guys, this was a new scene.
嗯，各位，这是一场新拍的戏。

100
00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:00.610
But we knew about it when we were shooting beach games.
但我们在拍摄《海滩游戏》时就已经知道这段剧情了。

101
00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:04.670
So we shot this during the beach games shoot.
所以我们是在拍摄“海滩游戏”那集时拍的这段。

102
00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:07.530
We did not have to go back to the dam.
我们没必要再回那个水坝去。

103
00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:08.070
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

104
00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.430
We couldn't get that location again.
我们没法再回到那个取景地了。

105
00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.110
So they shot it while we were there.
所以他们就在我们在那儿的时候顺便拍了。

106
00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.910
And, Jenna, I remember that they brought Ken Quapis to direct that.
而且，珍娜，我记得他们请了肯·夸皮斯来执导那场戏。

107
00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:16.950
And that was actually very common.
这其实非常普遍。

108
00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:19.510
That wasn't like anything weird to Harold Ramis.
对哈罗德·雷米斯来说这没什么奇怪的。

109
00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:25.910
That was really common on a show if you had a cross-board moment where you had a scene that was in another episode,
如果剧集里有跨集拍摄的情况，比如某场戏其实属于另一集，这在剧组里真的很常见，

110
00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:31.810
the director of that episode would come and direct that to sort of complete their story.
那一集的导演就会过来执导那场戏，算是补全他们的故事线。

111
00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:40.950
So Ken came back and, Jenna, I read that this was supposed to be in the beginning of the show, like the cold open.
所以肯回来了，而且珍娜，我读到过说这段原本是打算放在剧集开头，也就是冷开场里的。

112
00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:49.290
Yes, just like that jump from casino night to gay witch hunt, we were going to originally open this episode.
没错，就像从“赌场之夜”到“同性恋猎巫行动”的跳跃一样，我们原本打算用这个作为这集的开场。

113
00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:54.950
The cold open was going to be watching this scene between Jim and Pam on the beach.
冷开场原本是看吉姆和帕姆在海滩上的这段戏。

114
00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:56.790
I'm so glad it wasn't that way.
我真庆幸最后没那样做。

115
00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:00.670
I think it creates so much more tension.
我觉得这样处理制造了多得多的张力。

116
00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:01.550
Yeah.
没错。

117
00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:05.150
To leave it until later as a flashback.
把它留到后面作为闪回处理。

118
00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:13.810
And, you know, Jenna, it really did add to the tension because now we know as the audience that they had had this moment.
而且，你知道吗，珍娜，它确实增加了张力，因为现在作为观众，我们知道他们有过这一刻。

119
00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:21.290
And so when Pam is saying goodbye and good luck and all of that, it's layered with this moment that they shared at Beach Games.
所以当帕姆在说再见、祝你好运之类的客套话时，其中就叠加了他们在“海滩游戏”里分享的那一刻。

120
00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.650
And I love that our show did this.
我喜欢我们剧集这种处理方式。

121
00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.030
Our show didn't always just spoon feed the audience.
我们的剧集并不总是把信息直接喂给观众。

122
00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.930
It just had them like sort of pick up in the middle.
它只是让观众在中间阶段自己去领会。

123
00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.390
And I just loved it.
我真是太喜欢了。

124
00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:38.150
It was during the editing process that they decided to take it out of the cold open and put it later.
是在剪辑过程中，他们决定把它从冷开场里拿出来，放到后面去。

125
00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:45.450
Dave Rogers said in the DVD commentary that it was Mike Schur's idea to make it a flashback later in the episode.
戴夫·罗杰斯在DVD评论音轨里说，是迈克·舒尔的主意，把它改成了这集后半部分的闪回。

126
00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:46.830
I love that.
我喜欢这个点子。

127
00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:47.230
I know.
我也喜欢。

128
00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:47.910
He's so smart.
他太聪明了。

129
00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.090
He's such a smarty.
他真是个小机灵鬼。

130
00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:50.650
Fast fact number three.
冷知识第三条。

131
00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:52.810
Angela, I'm staying consistent today.
安吉拉，我今天保持着稳定的输出。

132
00:07:53.030 --> 00:08:01.430
It is a fan question from Faye B, Kayla Moffitt, Tiffany L, Brianna K, and Rowena C.
这是一个来自费伊·B、凯拉·莫菲特、蒂芙尼·L、布里安娜·K和罗威娜·C的粉丝提问。

133
00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:08.230
Did John and Rashida actually film in New York and how much of the crew was with them?
