00:28:46.350 --> 00:28:50.090
This is a secret that you should not allow Michael to hold.
这是一个你不该让迈克尔知道的秘密。

605
00:28:50.270 --> 00:28:52.430
You can't tell Michael any secret.
你不能告诉迈克尔任何秘密。

606
00:28:52.430 --> 00:28:57.950
You couldn't say, hey, don't tell anyone, but I have toe fungus.
你不能跟他说，嘿，别告诉别人，但我有脚趾真菌。

607
00:28:58.250 --> 00:28:59.010
Forget it.
算了吧。

608
00:28:59.450 --> 00:29:05.590
The next thing out of his mouth would be, I'm so sorry you have toe fungus in front of everyone.
他下一句脱口而出的肯定就是，我很抱歉你当着大家的面有脚趾真菌。

609
00:29:06.050 --> 00:29:06.550
Yes.
是的。

610
00:29:06.590 --> 00:29:07.950
I don't have toe fungus.
我没有脚趾真菌。

611
00:29:07.950 --> 00:29:09.330
I was just trying to think of something.
我只是随口想个例子。

612
00:29:09.590 --> 00:29:11.510
I have fungus on my toenails.
我的脚趾甲上有真菌。

613
00:29:11.730 --> 00:29:13.930
I know, but you treated it and it's all better.
我知道，但你已经治疗过了，现在全好了。

614
00:29:14.590 --> 00:29:15.790
It came back.
又复发了。

615
00:29:16.010 --> 00:29:16.690
It did?
是吗？

616
00:29:22.530 --> 00:29:26.570
A good amount of oxygen you can get in.
你能吸入相当多的氧气。

617
00:29:26.750 --> 00:29:31.230
You know, it's by the way, everyone, toe fungus is just like on your toenail.
顺便说一下，各位，脚趾真菌就是长在脚趾甲上的那种。

618
00:29:31.390 --> 00:29:33.050
It's just like a little white spot.
就像一个小小白点。

619
00:29:33.430 --> 00:29:33.570
Yeah.
是啊。

620
00:29:34.150 --> 00:29:35.550
That's what those white spots are.
那些白点就是这么来的。

621
00:29:35.670 --> 00:29:39.630
Everyone, if you're like, what are these white spots on my toenails when I take off my nail polish?
各位，如果你在想，为什么我卸掉指甲油后脚趾甲上有这些白点？

622
00:29:39.730 --> 00:29:40.750
That's toe fungus, y'all.
那可是脚趾真菌，伙计们。

623
00:29:40.930 --> 00:29:46.050
And you can get a special like oil and polish to put on there to get rid of it if you care.
如果你在意的话，可以买种特殊的油和指甲油涂上去，把它治好。

624
00:29:46.050 --> 00:29:51.150
Well, my mom always would say, every once in a while, just take your toenail polish off and let your toenails breathe.
嗯，我妈总是说，偶尔要把脚趾甲油卸掉，让脚趾甲透透气。

625
00:29:51.450 --> 00:29:52.230
It's good advice.
这是个好建议。

626
00:29:52.590 --> 00:29:53.390
It's not pretty.
但看起来不太好看。

627
00:29:53.610 --> 00:29:56.030
You're going to have a week of like funky looking yellow toes.
你会有一周的时间看着脚趾又黄又怪。

628
00:29:56.310 --> 00:29:56.570
Sorry.
抱歉。

629
00:29:58.390 --> 00:29:58.930
All right.
好吧。

630
00:29:59.030 --> 00:29:59.690
Sorry, sorry, sorry.
抱歉，抱歉，抱歉。

631
00:29:59.810 --> 00:30:00.430
Where are we?
我们说到哪了？

632
00:30:00.650 --> 00:30:04.970
Well, we need to go back to Dunder Mifflin because Dwight would like everyone to gather in the conference room.
嗯，我们需要回到邓德·米夫林，因为德怀特想让大家在会议室集合。

633
00:30:05.230 --> 00:30:10.710
He needs to discuss and introduce the Shrute Buck reward system.
他要讨论并介绍“施鲁特币”奖励系统。

634
00:30:13.620 --> 00:30:15.000
It was so funny to me.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

635
00:30:15.180 --> 00:30:16.600
You know what I loved about this?
你知道我喜欢这一段的什么吗？

636
00:30:16.600 --> 00:30:19.040
First of all, at 25 minutes, three seconds.
首先，在25分03秒的时候。

637
00:30:19.320 --> 00:30:20.480
Angela is so proud.
安吉拉感到非常自豪。

638
00:30:20.860 --> 00:30:22.000
She's so proud.
她太自豪了。

639
00:30:22.440 --> 00:30:23.500
She has this look.
她露出了那种表情。

640
00:30:23.740 --> 00:30:26.140
Dwight is calling his first conference room meeting.
德怀特正在召开他的第一次会议室会议。

641
00:30:26.220 --> 00:30:27.860
She can't believe it.
她简直不敢相信。

642
00:30:27.980 --> 00:30:30.140
But I love how he leads everyone in.
但我喜欢他带大家进去的方式。

643
00:30:30.240 --> 00:30:32.300
He's like, no more meetings, right?
他说，不再开会了，对吧？

644
00:30:32.420 --> 00:30:34.320
Michael had all these useless meetings.
迈克尔以前开了那么多没用的会。

645
00:30:34.840 --> 00:30:36.480
Instead, we're going to have lectures.
取而代之的是，我们要开始上课了。

646
00:30:37.940 --> 00:30:38.400
Yes.
没错。

647
00:30:39.020 --> 00:30:40.680
And Pam can't wait.
帕姆已经迫不及待了。

648
00:30:40.880 --> 00:30:41.840
She's like, what is he going to do?
她心想，他到底要干什么？

649
00:30:41.840 --> 00:30:42.480
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

650
00:30:42.580 --> 00:30:43.820
I can't wait to see what's about to happen.
我迫不及待想看看接下来会发生什么。

651
00:30:43.820 --> 00:30:47.380
Well, we get in there and we start getting our first lecture.
嗯，我们进去之后就开始听第一堂课了。

652
00:30:48.040 --> 00:30:52.800
And it is about the origin of papermaking.
讲的是造纸术的起源。

653
00:30:53.040 --> 00:30:53.160
Yeah.
是啊。

654
00:30:53.360 --> 00:30:58.780
He starts with a bunch of Tupperware tins full of soil, different types of soil.
他拿出一堆装满泥土的特百惠盒子，各种不同类型的土。

655
00:30:59.520 --> 00:31:07.620
And he asked the question, what would you say is the most important element in the production of above ground leafy growth?
然后他问了一个问题，你们觉得对于地上叶类植物的生长来说，最重要的元素是什么？

656
00:31:09.100 --> 00:31:10.980
You probably think it's phosphorus.
你们可能会觉得是磷。

657
00:31:11.460 --> 00:31:14.100
And then Angela secretly shakes her head no.
然后安吉拉偷偷摇了摇头，表示不是。

658
00:31:14.300 --> 00:31:15.740
I improvised that.
那是我即兴发挥的。

659
00:31:15.740 --> 00:31:18.860
And our camera operator caught it and was like, oh, that's so good.
我们的摄影师捕捉到了这一幕，觉得特别好。

660
00:31:19.060 --> 00:31:19.860
Ken loved it.
肯很喜欢。

661
00:31:19.960 --> 00:31:21.460
And he told me to keep doing it.
他让我继续那样做。

662
00:31:22.000 --> 00:31:22.980
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

663
00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:26.620
Like, I obviously knew this speech that Dwight had practiced it for me.
因为我显然知道德怀特为我练习过这段演讲。

664
00:31:26.740 --> 00:31:28.260
I used to love having those moments.
我以前很喜欢这种时刻。

665
00:31:28.640 --> 00:31:31.060
I'm sure he practiced it for you.
我敢肯定他为你练习过。

666
00:31:31.120 --> 00:31:31.420
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

667
00:31:31.420 --> 00:31:32.560
And he's killing it.
而且他表现得太棒了。

668
00:31:32.760 --> 00:31:35.460
According to you, you're like, he's killing it.
照你这么说，你当时觉得他表现得太棒了。

669
00:31:35.740 --> 00:31:36.660
Crushing it.
简直绝了。

670
00:31:36.660 --> 00:31:41.100
By the way, the answer is nitrogen, per Dwight.
顺便说一下，根据德怀特的说法，答案是氮。

671
00:31:41.820 --> 00:31:43.520
Lady, I had to know.
大姐，我得知道答案啊。

672
00:31:43.700 --> 00:31:44.720
Did you look it up?
你去查了吗？

673
00:31:44.820 --> 00:31:45.940
Did you look up phosphorus?
你去查磷了吗？

674
00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:49.100
You know that website Quora?
你知道Quora那个网站吗？

675
00:31:49.640 --> 00:31:49.760
Yeah.
知道。

676
00:31:49.920 --> 00:31:54.800
It's where you post a question about something and then experts on that subject weigh in.
就是你在上面发布一个问题，然后该领域的专家会给出解答。

677
00:31:54.980 --> 00:31:56.160
Did you post the question?
你发那个问题了吗？

678
00:31:56.900 --> 00:31:58.520
I didn't post the question.
我没发那个问题。

679
00:31:58.520 --> 00:31:59.580
Oh, I got real excited.
哦，我刚才还特别兴奋呢。

680
00:31:59.980 --> 00:32:04.240
But years ago, someone posted that exact question.
但几年前，有人发布过一模一样的问题。

681
00:32:04.240 --> 00:32:05.960
The wording was exact.
措辞都一模一样。

682
00:32:06.900 --> 00:32:08.560
Exactly what Dwight says.
和德怀特说的一字不差。

683
00:32:08.720 --> 00:32:12.340
There was an office fan years ago that was like, wait, is this true?
几年前有个《办公室》的粉丝发帖问，等等，这是真的吗？

684
00:32:12.600 --> 00:32:21.260
So it's really amazing the back and forth from all the people who are not realizing that this is a direct quote from an office episode.
所以看到那些完全没意识到这是《办公室》剧集原话的人在下面争论，真的太有意思了。

685
00:32:21.260 --> 00:32:25.780
It is just soil scientists weighing in.
全是土壤科学家在发表意见。

686
00:32:25.920 --> 00:32:26.800
There's charts.
还有图表。

687
00:32:27.420 --> 00:32:36.060
There's pages and pages of these scientists debating what is the most important element in the production of above ground leafy growth.
有整整好几页的科学家在争论到底什么才是地上叶类植物生长最重要的元素。

688
00:32:36.300 --> 00:32:39.320
And the consensus is nitrogen.
最后的共识是氮。

689
00:32:40.300 --> 00:32:41.020
Huh.
哈。

690
00:32:41.140 --> 00:32:41.480
Nitrogen.
氮。

691
00:32:42.240 --> 00:32:43.240
Way to go, Dwight.
干得好，德怀特。

692
00:32:43.680 --> 00:32:45.120
Way to go.
干得好。

693
00:32:45.640 --> 00:32:47.800
Jenna, do you remember filming the scene?
珍娜，你还记得拍那场戏吗？

694
00:32:47.800 --> 00:32:49.100
Because I remember the smell.
因为我记得那股味道。

695
00:32:49.460 --> 00:32:50.820
Can we talk about it for a second?
我们能聊聊这个吗？

696
00:32:51.080 --> 00:32:51.660
We can.
可以。

697
00:32:52.160 --> 00:32:54.160
There was an earthy smell.
有一股泥土味。

698
00:32:54.340 --> 00:32:56.080
Now, you know this room had no real windows.
你要知道，那个房间没有真正的窗户。

699
00:32:56.160 --> 00:32:57.580
So it's like sitting in a box.
就像坐在一个盒子里一样。

700
00:32:57.700 --> 00:33:01.560
Now, it didn't have a full ceiling, but we were sort of trapped in there with smells.
虽然没有完全封顶，但我们确实被困在里面，闻着那些味道。

701
00:33:02.600 --> 00:33:03.220
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

702
00:33:03.220 --> 00:33:06.420
And there was a real dirt smell.
而且当时真的有一股泥土味。

703
00:33:06.660 --> 00:33:08.880
And then it's in the deleted scenes.
后来那段被剪掉了。

704
00:33:08.880 --> 00:33:10.320
You guys don't get to see it.
你们没机会看到了。

705
00:33:10.420 --> 00:33:13.720
But Dwight actually starts by dumping a whole bunch of trash on the table.
但德怀特其实一开始就在桌上倒了一大堆垃圾。

706
00:33:13.880 --> 00:33:14.900
I remember that.
我记得那个。

707
00:33:15.100 --> 00:33:17.180
To talk to everyone about recycling.
为了跟大伙儿谈谈回收利用的事。

708
00:33:17.600 --> 00:33:21.060
So we had some earthy, trashy smells going.
所以当时现场弥漫着一股泥土和垃圾味。

709
00:33:21.880 --> 00:33:22.440
Yeah.
没错。

710
00:33:22.640 --> 00:33:23.520
It was intense.
味道很重。

711
00:33:23.540 --> 00:33:31.780
We also have the great moment, which is one of my favorite moments, where Stanley does not want to participate.
我们还有一个很棒的片段，也是我最喜欢的片段之一，就是斯坦利不想参与其中。

712
00:33:32.640 --> 00:33:36.140
He won a shroot buck, but he doesn't want it.
他赢了一张施鲁特币，但他不想要。

713
00:33:36.340 --> 00:33:37.640
No, he doesn't want it.
没错，他不想要。

714
00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:39.720
He does not want to participate in any of this.
他根本不想参与这些事。

715
00:33:39.920 --> 00:33:42.520
And Dwight is like, you don't want your shroot buck?
德怀特就问，你不要你的施鲁特币吗？

716
00:33:42.740 --> 00:33:44.140
And he's like, no.
他说，不要。

717
00:33:45.140 --> 00:33:49.440
And then he offers him like a thousand Stanley Nichols to leave him alone.
然后他提出给德怀特一千个斯坦利镍币，只求德怀特别再烦他。

718
00:33:49.660 --> 00:33:50.020
A billion.
是一十亿。

719
00:33:50.160 --> 00:33:54.760
A billion Stanley Nichols if you never speak to me again.
如果你永远别再跟我说话，我就给你十亿个斯坦利镍币。

720
00:33:55.440 --> 00:33:55.940
Yes.
没错。

721
00:33:56.080 --> 00:33:56.640
Thank you.
谢谢。

722
00:33:56.800 --> 00:33:57.480
It's brilliant.
太绝了。

723
00:33:57.920 --> 00:34:02.940
And Dwight's response is he would like to know the conversion rate between Stanley Nichols and shroot bucks.
德怀特的反应是他想知道斯坦利镍币和施鲁特币的汇率。

724
00:34:04.300 --> 00:34:07.340
And it's the same as leprechauns to unicorns.
结果汇率和矮妖精对独角兽的汇率一样。

725
00:34:07.380 --> 00:34:07.460
Yeah.
没错。

726
00:34:07.780 --> 00:34:09.780
And then, Jenna, you must have had so much fun.
然后呢，珍娜，你当时一定玩得很开心吧。

727
00:34:09.920 --> 00:34:12.580
Because then everyone starts to be like, I'm out of here.
因为接着大家就开始说，我不干了。

728
00:34:12.580 --> 00:34:13.340
I don't want to do this.
我不想做这个。

729
00:34:13.340 --> 00:34:17.440
And Pam is like, hey, pay attention.
然后帕姆就说，嘿，注意听。

730
00:34:19.180 --> 00:34:21.400
Lady, when I heard that delivery.
天哪，当我听到那句台词时。

731
00:34:21.580 --> 00:34:24.120
Now, this was before I had children.
那时候我还没生孩子。

732
00:34:24.560 --> 00:34:33.360
But when I heard my voice, I was like, oh, my gosh, that's the voice when I have to lay down the law with the kids.
但当我听到自己的声音时，我心想，天呐，那简直就是我管教孩子时的语气。

733
00:34:33.480 --> 00:34:34.800
When I'm like, listen to me.
就像我说，听着。

734
00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:38.500
I've asked three times to brush our teeth.
我已经说了三遍要刷牙了。

735
00:34:38.720 --> 00:34:40.060
It's time to brush teeth.
该去刷牙了。

736
00:34:40.240 --> 00:34:41.160
Now, hustle.
快点。

737
00:34:41.460 --> 00:34:42.660
Go to the bathroom.
去洗手间。

738
00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:46.380
I was like, oh, my gosh, that is my mom voice.
我当时就想，天呐，那就是我的“妈妈嗓”。

739
00:34:46.880 --> 00:34:47.860
That's my mom voice.
那就是我的“妈妈嗓”。

740
00:34:47.880 --> 00:34:49.580
That's your mom getting line voice.
那是你妈妈在排队时的声音。

741
00:34:50.120 --> 00:34:51.000
Yeah, that's right.
没错，就是那样。

742
00:34:51.200 --> 00:34:51.400
Yeah.
没错。

743
00:34:51.880 --> 00:34:52.540
For sure.
确实。

744
00:34:52.540 --> 00:34:53.300
I was shocked.
我当时都惊呆了。

745
00:34:53.740 --> 00:34:55.580
You had it in you all along.
原来你一直都有这种潜质。

746
00:34:55.800 --> 00:34:56.520
I did.
确实。

747
00:34:56.560 --> 00:34:57.780
It was meant to be.
这是命中注定的。

748
00:34:58.000 --> 00:35:01.060
Well, there's a nice little moment that I think Phyllis just improvised.
嗯，有个不错的小片段，我觉得是菲利斯即兴发挥的。

749
00:35:01.200 --> 00:35:03.440
And we often did things like this in the background.
我们经常在背景里做这类事。

750
00:35:03.440 --> 00:35:08.980
We just sort of made up our own story if we didn't have dialogue of how we would react to these moments.
如果没有台词，我们就会自己编故事，决定在这些时刻该有什么反应。

751
00:35:09.480 --> 00:35:10.740
And she's sleeping.
她睡着了。

752
00:35:11.360 --> 00:35:12.160
I know.
我知道。

753
00:35:13.300 --> 00:35:15.260
27 minutes, 29 seconds.
27分29秒。

754
00:35:15.780 --> 00:35:19.570
I thought that was an amazing choice.
我觉得那是个很棒的选择。

755
00:35:19.730 --> 00:35:19.830
Yeah.
是啊。

756
00:35:19.830 --> 00:35:20.790
An amazing choice.
很棒的选择。

757
00:35:21.790 --> 00:35:24.290
Well, listen, lady, we're about to go back to corporate.
好吧，听着，女士，我们马上要回到公司的话题了。

758
00:35:24.630 --> 00:35:27.230
We're going to see Karen interview with David.
我们要去看凯伦接受大卫的面试。

759
00:35:27.350 --> 00:35:29.170
But I think we should take a break.
但我认为我们应该休息一下。

760
00:35:29.350 --> 00:35:32.870
I think we should take a break and come back because Karen is crushing her interview.
我觉得我们应该休息一下再回来，因为凯伦的面试表现太出色了。

761
00:35:33.150 --> 00:35:34.230
We need to get to it.
我们得接着聊这个。

762
00:35:34.230 --> 00:35:35.250
She's doing really well.
她表现得非常好。

763
00:35:35.410 --> 00:35:35.590
Yeah.
是啊。

764
00:35:36.030 --> 00:35:36.350
All right.
好吧。

765
00:35:36.430 --> 00:35:37.130
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

766
00:35:45.880 --> 00:35:46.320
Okay.
好的。

767
00:35:46.420 --> 00:35:47.720
We are back from break.
我们休息回来了。

768
