Like her emotions are going up and down.
她的情绪起伏太大了。

1081
00:50:02.830 --> 00:50:06.270
She's like, I could wear stretch pants and wait for you to come home at 515.
她说，我可以穿着紧身裤，等着你五点十五分回家。

1082
00:50:07.570 --> 00:50:07.970
Yes.
没错。

1083
00:50:08.210 --> 00:50:11.770
She invites herself to move in with Michael.
她自作主张要搬去和迈克尔一起住。

1084
00:50:12.070 --> 00:50:12.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1085
00:50:12.410 --> 00:50:13.770
And Michael is like, what?
而迈克尔的反应是，什么？

1086
00:50:14.610 --> 00:50:15.010
Oh.
哦。

1087
00:50:15.330 --> 00:50:16.770
Well, he, come on.
好吧，他，得了吧。

1088
00:50:16.890 --> 00:50:18.090
He walked himself into that.
是他自己掉进坑里的。

1089
00:50:18.210 --> 00:50:21.530
He's like, I guess you could move in with me in my condo.
他说，我想你可以搬进我的公寓跟我一起住。

1090
00:50:21.610 --> 00:50:22.570
I guess I could get it back.
我想我能把它拿回来。

1091
00:50:22.570 --> 00:50:25.350
I'd probably get a negative review on my eBay account.
我可能会在我的eBay账户上收到差评。

1092
00:50:26.630 --> 00:50:29.650
But it's like at the beginning of this episode,
但这集刚开始的时候，

1093
00:50:30.370 --> 00:50:35.450
he asks all of the ladies to help him not get back together with Jan.
他请求所有的女士帮他不要和简复合。

1094
00:50:35.590 --> 00:50:38.470
And it ends with them moving in together.
结果却是他们搬到了一起住。

1095
00:50:38.970 --> 00:50:39.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1096
00:50:39.930 --> 00:50:41.550
And she doesn't have a job.
而且她还没工作。

1097
00:50:41.750 --> 00:50:42.750
And she's spiraling.
她正在失控。

1098
00:50:44.050 --> 00:50:44.970
It's a lot.
这信息量太大了。

1099
00:50:46.590 --> 00:50:48.430
Well, Michael comes back into the office.
好吧，迈克尔回到了办公室。

1100
00:50:48.750 --> 00:50:52.270
He announces he has withdrawn his name from contention.
他宣布他已经退出了竞选。

1101
00:50:53.390 --> 00:50:57.010
He notices that his office is now painted black.
他注意到他的办公室现在被漆成了黑色。

1102
00:50:57.310 --> 00:50:57.650
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1103
00:50:58.870 --> 00:51:00.250
I liked this bit.
我喜欢这一段。

1104
00:51:00.650 --> 00:51:02.790
He tells Ryan to go get him a coffee.
他让瑞安去给他买杯咖啡。

1105
00:51:02.810 --> 00:51:04.810
And Ryan said he doesn't do that stuff anymore.
瑞安说他不再做那种事了。

1106
00:51:05.150 --> 00:51:07.410
And he says, no, it's for me, bimbo.
他说，不，这是给我买的，笨蛋。

1107
00:51:07.910 --> 00:51:08.470
Kids.
现在的孩子。

1108
00:51:08.650 --> 00:51:08.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1109
00:51:09.290 --> 00:51:09.970
I know.
我知道。

1110
00:51:10.450 --> 00:51:12.470
Oh, Ryan is about to have his moment.
哦，瑞安的高光时刻要来了。

1111
00:51:13.270 --> 00:51:17.590
And this is when Pam asks, did Karen get the job?
这时帕姆问，凯伦得到那份工作了吗？

1112
00:51:19.070 --> 00:51:19.710
Hmm.
嗯。

1113
00:51:20.410 --> 00:51:20.750
Yeah.
是啊。

1114
00:51:20.750 --> 00:51:21.070
I don't know.
我不知道。

1115
00:51:21.270 --> 00:51:22.250
Someone's real curious.
有人真的很好奇。

1116
00:51:22.770 --> 00:51:26.050
Michael has a whole speech here that is sort of heartbreaking.
迈克尔在这里有一大段演讲，听起来有点令人心碎。

1117
00:51:26.050 --> 00:51:28.690
He says, yeah, so I'm going nowhere.
他说，是啊，所以我哪儿也不去。

1118
00:51:29.330 --> 00:51:30.850
Never going to leave.
永远不会离开。

1119
00:51:31.030 --> 00:51:38.890
This place is going to be the hospital where I was born, my house, my old age home, my graveyard for my bones.
这个地方将成为我出生时的医院、我的家、我的养老院，以及我埋骨的墓地。

1120
00:51:38.890 --> 00:51:44.710
And the camera pans across everyone's faces like, this isn't good news for anybody.
镜头扫过每个人的脸，仿佛在说，这对任何人来说都不是好消息。

1121
00:51:45.530 --> 00:51:46.850
Yeah, it's true.
是啊，确实如此。

1122
00:51:47.110 --> 00:51:49.070
And then Dwight's back at his desk.
然后德怀特回到了他的办公桌前。

1123
00:51:49.630 --> 00:51:50.870
This is a sweet moment.
这是一个温馨的时刻。

1124
00:51:51.110 --> 00:51:58.270
I love these sweet moments between Pam and Dwight where he thanks Pam for serving with great dignity.
我喜欢帕姆和德怀特之间这些温馨的时刻，他感谢帕姆以极大的尊严与他共事。

1125
00:51:58.770 --> 00:52:01.770
And she salutes him and he salutes her back.
她向他敬礼，他也回敬了她。

1126
00:52:02.170 --> 00:52:02.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1127
00:52:02.830 --> 00:52:04.790
It's kind of their version of the air high five.
这算是他们版本的空中击掌吧。

1128
00:52:05.230 --> 00:52:08.750
Well, you know, Dwight goes on to say eventually that Pam is his best friend.
嗯，你知道，德怀特后来终于说帕姆是他最好的朋友。

1129
00:52:09.050 --> 00:52:09.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1130
00:52:09.890 --> 00:52:10.350
I know.
我知道。

1131
00:52:10.770 --> 00:52:11.910
It's so sweet.
太温馨了。

1132
00:52:12.470 --> 00:52:15.790
Well, this is something that probably most people didn't catch.
嗯，这是大多数人可能没注意到的细节。

1133
00:52:15.930 --> 00:52:21.250
But at 35 minutes, 34 seconds in the background and accounting, Brian,
但在35分34秒时，在会计部的背景里，布莱恩，

1134
00:52:21.410 --> 00:52:26.790
as Kevin sort of improvises this moment when Michael saying that he's back and he's like doing all that weird stuff.
当凯文即兴发挥这一幕时，迈克尔说他回来了，还在做那些奇怪的动作。

1135
00:52:26.790 --> 00:52:28.650
He's like, I'm back, right?
他说，我回来了，对吧？

1136
00:52:28.950 --> 00:52:29.230
Yes.
是的。

1137
00:52:29.390 --> 00:52:29.670
Yes.
是的。

1138
00:52:29.910 --> 00:52:30.610
It's good.
挺好的。

1139
00:52:30.970 --> 00:52:31.670
I'm back.
我回来了。

1140
00:52:31.870 --> 00:52:36.250
Anyway, Kevin sort of leans over to Angela and Brian improvised this.
总之，凯文凑过去对安吉拉说了些什么，这是布莱恩即兴发挥的。

1141
00:52:36.370 --> 00:52:37.930
He was like, so wait, did he get the job?
他当时说，等等，他得到那份工作了吗？

1142
00:52:38.070 --> 00:52:39.070
And I just shake my head.
我只是摇了摇头。

1143
00:52:39.670 --> 00:52:40.110
No.
没有。

1144
00:52:40.630 --> 00:52:42.210
And you can't hear what he's saying.
你听不到他在说什么。

1145
00:52:42.210 --> 00:52:44.290
I just remember these little moments like that.
我只记得这些小瞬间。

1146
00:52:44.410 --> 00:52:48.090
And we just were having our own scene back there.
我们在后面演着我们自己的戏。

1147
00:52:48.650 --> 00:52:49.670
I love those.
我喜欢这些瞬间。

1148
00:52:50.570 --> 00:52:51.790
We're always acting.
我们一直在演戏。

1149
00:52:52.110 --> 00:52:52.770
You never know.
你永远不知道。

1150
00:52:52.890 --> 00:52:53.670
You never know.
你永远不知道。

1151
00:52:53.670 --> 00:52:54.410
What the camera's getting.
摄像机拍到的画面。

1152
00:52:54.630 --> 00:52:55.710
You never know.
谁也说不准。

1153
00:52:56.870 --> 00:52:58.530
Well, now we go to Jim's interview.
好了，现在我们来看看吉姆的面试。

1154
00:52:59.290 --> 00:53:00.330
He's a shoo-in.
他稳操胜券了。

1155
00:53:00.970 --> 00:53:03.430
David Wallace is like falling all over him.
大卫·华莱士简直对他青睐有加。

1156
00:53:04.090 --> 00:53:04.270
Yeah.
没错。

1157
00:53:05.050 --> 00:53:08.350
I mean, David Wallace should have started the interview by saying you're hired.
我是说，大卫·华莱士面试一开始就该直接说你被录用了。

1158
00:53:08.950 --> 00:53:12.850
David Wallace should have started the interview by saying, will you be my best friend?
大卫·华莱士面试一开始就该问，你愿意做我最好的朋友吗？

1159
00:53:13.450 --> 00:53:14.450
It's so true.
太对了。

1160
00:53:15.150 --> 00:53:16.810
Everybody wants Jim to be their best friend.
每个人都想让吉姆做他们最好的朋友。

1161
00:53:17.950 --> 00:53:19.530
He's a very likable guy.
他是个很讨人喜欢的人。

1162
00:53:19.770 --> 00:53:19.890
He's a good best friend.
他是个很好的挚友。

1163
00:53:20.230 --> 00:53:20.590
Yeah.
没错。

1164
00:53:20.850 --> 00:53:21.870
He's a great guy.
他是个很棒的人。

1165
00:53:22.070 --> 00:53:22.250
Yeah.
没错。

1166
00:53:22.250 --> 00:53:26.890
So David's asking him a few questions and he says, what is your favorite thing?
大卫问了他几个问题，然后问他，你最喜欢什么？

1167
00:53:26.990 --> 00:53:29.130
What do you like most about the Scranton office?
你最喜欢斯克兰顿分公司的哪一点？

1168
00:53:30.270 --> 00:53:37.650
And it's right at this moment that Jim opens up his little folder and there is like a note
就在那一刻，吉姆打开了他的小文件夹，里面有一张

1169
00:53:37.650 --> 00:53:45.710
of encouragement from Pam, along with a little yogurt lid that she has saved since office Olympics.
帕姆写的鼓励字条，还有她从办公室奥运会开始就一直留着的酸奶盖。

1170
00:53:46.110 --> 00:53:47.950
You know what that note says to me?
你知道那张字条对我来说意味着什么吗？

1171
00:53:48.690 --> 00:53:49.250
What?
什么？

1172
00:53:49.430 --> 00:53:52.250
I would have waited for you until after your interview.
我会等你面试结束的。

1173
00:53:54.870 --> 00:53:59.010
I wouldn't have gone and met my friends for a boozy lunch somewhere.
我才不会去和朋友们找个地方喝得烂醉吃午饭呢。

1174
00:53:59.830 --> 00:54:00.390
Exactly.
没错。

1175
00:54:01.070 --> 00:54:02.330
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

1176
00:54:02.490 --> 00:54:02.890
Thank you.
谢谢。

1177
00:54:03.090 --> 00:54:03.570
You matter.
你很重要。

1178
00:54:03.790 --> 00:54:05.590
And what happens to you matters to me.
你所经历的一切对我来说都很重要。

1179
00:54:06.330 --> 00:54:06.590
Yeah.
没错。

1180
00:54:08.590 --> 00:54:15.270
And Jim looks at that and he says his favorite thing about the Scranton office were the friendships.
吉姆看着字条说，他最喜欢斯克兰顿分公司的一点就是这里的友谊。

1181
00:54:16.790 --> 00:54:20.350
And that's when David asks him, where do you see yourself in 10 years?
就在这时，大卫问他，你十年后打算做什么？

1182
00:54:20.690 --> 00:54:22.150
Well, Jim is rattled now.
好吧，吉姆现在心乱了。

1183
00:54:22.350 --> 00:54:24.590
He had all these answers ready to go.
他原本准备好了所有答案。

1184
00:54:25.130 --> 00:54:30.290
I'm sure he had prepared for this interview, but now Pam is there with him.
我敢肯定他为这次面试做了准备，但现在帕姆就在他身边。

1185
00:54:31.250 --> 00:54:31.770
Yeah.
没错。

1186
00:54:31.930 --> 00:54:33.750
And we flash back to the beach.
镜头闪回到海滩。

1187
00:54:34.690 --> 00:54:38.370
And we hear Jim tells Pam why he left Scranton.
我们听到吉姆告诉帕姆他为什么离开斯克兰顿。

1188
00:54:38.590 --> 00:54:41.710
He acknowledges he's never really come back.
他承认自己从未真正回来过。

1189
00:54:42.110 --> 00:54:45.070
And then Pam, talk about some Pam sass.
然后帕姆，谈谈帕姆的犀利表现。

1190
00:54:45.250 --> 00:54:47.050
I thought this was super ballsy.
我觉得这真是太有胆量了。

1191
00:54:47.150 --> 00:54:49.090
She's like, well, I wish you would.
她说，好吧，我希望你能回来。

1192
00:54:49.710 --> 00:54:50.090
Whoa!
哇！

1193
00:54:51.130 --> 00:54:51.490
Yeah.
没错。

1194
00:54:51.750 --> 00:54:56.150
Well, now we sort of hear Jim's interview.
现在我们算是听到了吉姆的面试内容。

1195
00:54:56.510 --> 00:54:59.870
We hear like he's distracted.
听起来他心不在焉的。

1196
00:54:59.870 --> 00:55:01.470
He's making jokes.
他在开玩笑。

1197
00:55:02.090 --> 00:55:09.130
We cut to a Pam talking head where she explains she hasn't really heard anything.
镜头切到帕姆的采访，她解释说她还没收到任何消息。

1198
00:55:10.050 --> 00:55:11.870
Jim probably got the job.
吉姆大概是拿到这份工作了。

1199
00:55:12.090 --> 00:55:14.650
You know, there's no reason for him not to get the job.
你知道的，他没理由拿不到这份工作。

1200
00:55:16.030 --> 00:55:22.870
And she's, she's really like, you can see her trying to process it and stay really positive.
她看起来，你能看出她在努力消化这件事，并保持积极乐观。

1201
00:55:23.230 --> 00:55:24.330
She's all day.
她整天都这样。

1202
00:55:24.550 --> 00:55:31.990
She's been trying to stay really positive about this and convincing herself that her and Jim are friends.
她一直努力保持积极心态，说服自己她和吉姆只是朋友。

1203
00:55:31.990 --> 00:55:33.470
This is in the paSt.
那都已经过去了。

1204
00:55:33.610 --> 00:55:35.030
The beach was just closure.
海滩那次只是为了做个了结。

1205
00:55:35.030 --> 00:55:36.530
That was closure.
那才是了结。

1206
00:55:37.350 --> 00:55:42.830
And, you know, she says, we just never got the timing right.
而且，你知道，她说，我们只是从来没在对的时间遇上。

1207
00:55:43.030 --> 00:55:44.190
And that's okay.
没关系。

1208
00:55:44.530 --> 00:55:46.150
And then Jim walks in the room.
然后吉姆走进房间。

1209
00:55:46.590 --> 00:55:49.330
I mean, she's so surprised to see him.
我是说，她看到他非常惊讶。

1210
00:55:49.630 --> 00:55:49.750
Yeah.
没错。

1211
00:55:49.830 --> 00:55:54.690
He interrupts the talking head and asks her if she wants to have dinner.
他打断了她的采访，问她愿不愿意一起吃晚饭。

1212
00:55:54.870 --> 00:55:55.970
She says, yeah.
她说，好啊。

1213
00:55:56.210 --> 00:55:57.930
And then he's like, it's a date.
然后他说，这是约会。

1214
00:55:57.930 --> 00:56:02.890
Jenna, many, many people have talked about how great you are in that moment.
珍娜，很多人都说你在那一刻表现得太棒了。

1215
00:56:02.890 --> 00:56:03.830
And you are.
你确实很棒。

1216
00:56:03.990 --> 00:56:04.650
You are.
真的。

1217
00:56:04.790 --> 00:56:06.970
You are so good in that moment.
你在那一刻表现得太好了。

1218
00:56:07.230 --> 00:56:10.950
So many emotions go across your face and your eyes tear up.
你的脸上闪过无数种情绪，眼眶也湿润了。

1219
00:56:11.370 --> 00:56:12.810
Ken Quappas said you made him cry.
肯·夸帕斯说你让他看哭了。

1220
00:56:13.030 --> 00:56:14.170
Well, here's the thing.
嗯，是这样的。

1221
00:56:14.990 --> 00:56:18.230
I owe that moment to Ken Quappas.
那一刻我得归功于肯·夸帕斯。

1222
00:56:18.230 --> 00:56:19.890
And I'll tell you why.
我来告诉你为什么。

1223
00:56:20.070 --> 00:56:26.270
A lot of people wrote in and wanted to know what was going through my head during that scene when Jim finally asked Pam out.
很多人写信来问，当吉姆终于约帕姆出去时，那一幕我心里在想什么。

1224
00:56:28.640 --> 00:56:36.540
It's crazy because Ken Quappas, he was a type of father figure to us, right, Angela?
这很疯狂，因为肯·夸帕斯，他就像我们的父亲一样，对吧，安吉拉？

1225
00:56:36.700 --> 00:56:42.340
When he was on the podcast, he explained that his technique is to love people into their best work.
当他上播客时，他解释说他的技巧是用爱去引导人们发挥出最好的水平。

1226
00:56:42.520 --> 00:56:45.460
He's just a very gentle, kind soul.
他是一个非常温柔、善良的人。

1227
00:56:45.680 --> 00:56:47.560
He's so, so kind.
他真的、真的非常善良。

1228
00:56:48.380 --> 00:56:50.500
I'm going to cry just thinking about it.
光是想到这一点我就要哭了。

1229
00:56:50.640 --> 00:56:55.520
I think, and I don't know, but I think we got that on the first take.
我想，我不确定，但我认为我们一条就过了。

1230
00:56:55.720 --> 00:56:58.260
I think what you are watching is the first take.
我想你们看到的正是第一条拍摄的画面。

1231
00:56:58.420 --> 00:56:58.960
Oh, wow.
哇。

1232
00:56:59.120 --> 00:57:06.620
Because we had kind of planned it out with the camera when it was going to swish over and when it was going to come back to me.
因为我们和摄影师提前规划好了，摄像机什么时候扫过去，什么时候扫回来对着我。

1233
00:57:06.880 --> 00:57:15.440
So in that moment when the camera swishes back to me, I was actually looking at Ken Quappas and he had tears in his eyes.
所以当摄像机扫回我这里时，我其实是在看着肯·夸帕斯，他当时眼含热泪。

1234
00:57:15.440 --> 00:57:17.600
And that made me tear up.
那让我也不禁热泪盈眶。

1235
00:57:17.680 --> 00:57:24.340
And we just shared this moment, this private moment of acknowledgement for this journey of this character.
我们分享了那一刻，那是属于我们私下的时刻，是对这个角色旅程的一种认可。

1236
00:57:24.500 --> 00:57:30.340
And he smiled at me in a way that a parent smiles at you when they're proud of you.
他对我微笑的样子，就像父母为你感到骄傲时那样。

1237
00:57:30.800 --> 00:57:40.080
